Canonical design: `solutions/international-investigation.json` and `docs/security-integrations/international-investigation.md`.
Keep status planned and executable false. Link existing agency solutions without creating an executable international tool, external channel connector or credential. Fund must pin reviewed commit and bytes.
Domestic case/source custody and receiving jurisdiction authority remain independent. Bind shared materials to recipient, purpose, immutable proposal/manifest digest, classification, storage, retention/onward-sharing conditions, expiry and channel. Changes and revocation invalidate approval.
Separate dispatch/receipt/integrity/recipient authority and technical verification/judicial admissibility. Preserve unknown and partial outcomes; reconcile operation/official receipt before retry. Record future-access revocation and recipient notification without claiming recall of exported bytes.
Use existing signed local evaluation packages with externally approved trust and separately reviewed translations; do not invent institutional identity or universal signature interoperability. Separate police/prosecution/counsel/defense/judicial roles and confidential data. Public directories and templates do not submit cases. No new remote MCP, native sync or automatic upload is implied.
